--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. FORMAL PATENT PENDING NOTICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The cyber-physical architectures, hardware abstraction mechanisms, state 
machines, and cryptographic validation routines disclosed or implemented 
herein are subject to an active patent examination process before the Patent 
Office of the Republic of Poland (Urząd Patentowy Rzeczypospolitej Polskiej - UPRP):

  * Patent Application Number: P.454742
  * Filing Date: February 13, 2026
  * Jurisdiction: Republic of Poland (with Paris Convention priority rights 
    explicitly reserved for international PCT filings)
  * Title / Scope: System, method, and protocol for cryptographically anchored 
    offline transaction timestamping and hardware-verified authorization 
    (T-OTP: Trusted Offline Transaction Protocol).

PROTECTED INVENTIONS & CLAIMS COVER:
  a) Hardware Time Oracle (Sprzętowa Wyrocznia Czasu): Direct acquisition and 
     cryptographic binding of monotonic hardware timestamps generated by sealed, 
     tamper-evident Real-Time Clock (RTC) modules integrated into fiscal memory 
     units certified and homologated by the Central Office of Measures 
     (Główny Urząd Miar - GUM), operating strictly isolated from the host OS.
  b) Localchain (Niezmienny Rejestr Lokalny): Sequential cryptographic chaining 
     (SHA-256) linking zero-connectivity transactions into an immutable, 
     backward-linked micro-ledger residing on local storage.
  c) Hard Lock Controller (Kontroler Blokady Twardej): Logical and physical 
     interlocking mechanisms that halt paper ejection, receipt completion, and 
     Point of Sale (POS) transaction state transitions until the cryptographic 
     "Frozen Blob" is committed to non-volatile memory.
  d) Moment of Freezing Protocol: Algorithmic offline validation procedures 
     enabling non-fiscal entitlements (e-prescriptions, healthcare authorizations) 
     to be executed securely during network partitions (up to 24 hours) and 
     verified deterministically by central repositories (CROK, P1 / e-Zdrowie).

